17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197837 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "16556c36-9687-51db-b717-e19ba445257b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197838 #edb/ref 1080 "$(3,-1,-1)$ and $(-3, 1, 1)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197838 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197838 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1b935e3d-9066-54d6-bc61-c08323d32d91" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197839 #edb/ref 1080 "$(3, 1, 1)$ and $(-3,-1,-1)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197839 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197839 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "27b5c930-f165-5810-bfa0-aefe2f7b3378" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197858 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186197859 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197858 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186197860 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197858 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186197861 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197858 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186197862 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197858 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186197863 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197858 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197858 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197858 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "34ed6a25-4fb8-5bc4-ae1e-17b36f0b19cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197859 #edb/ref 1080 "$(0, 1, 2)$ only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197859 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197859 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "85f15136-5f32-5a95-ad2e-c03583a57949" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197860 #edb/ref 1080 "$(1, 0, 3)$ only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197860 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197860 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a4489fee-7f97-564e-bfdf-100bd23a30ed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197861 #edb/ref 1080 "$(6,-5, 8)$ only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197861 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197861 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b0728ffd-9699-5c90-b8ee-e3dac68240ef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197862 #edb/ref 1080 "$(0, 1, 2)$ and $(1, 0, 3)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197862 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197862 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b3c89d68-81f7-58e3-821d-8b592946c252" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197863 #edb/ref 1080 "$(-1, 2, 1)$ and $(1, 0, 3)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197863 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186197863 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "27cb9b6f-8c13-5194-b996-a553a94b44ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198075 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12558" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198075 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the points of the intersection of the elliptic cone $x^2 + y^2=z^2$ and the line $x +1=y-1 =\\dfrac{z}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198075 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "89942534-6b03-52ec-8494-830de5eb8128" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198075 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we write the equation of our line in the parametric form:\n![](images/41/41e6a96cc57d9ce57d5a7bec35586175d9217f92e4dc2bab106db641db9f24ea.png)\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\nSubstituting the above expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ (t-1)^{2}+(t+1)^{2} & =(2t)^{2} \\\\ {t}^{2}-2t+1+{t}^{2}+2t+1 & =4{t}^{2} \\\\ 2{t}^{2}+2 & =4{t}^{2} \\\\ 2 & =2{t}^{2} \\\\ {t}^{2} & =1 \\\\ t & =\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=-1,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1-1=-2 \\\\ y=-1+1=0 \\\\ z=2(-1)=-2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $\\left(-2,0,-2\\right).$\n\n- For $t=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1-1=0 \\\\ y=1+1=2 \\\\ z=2(1)=2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $\\left(0,2,2\\right).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(-2,0,-2)$ and $(0,2,2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198228 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5264" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198228 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the ellipsoid $\\dfrac{x^2}{24} + \\dfrac{y^2}{24} +\\dfrac{z^2}{6} = 1$ and the line \n${\\begin{aligned}x=4t \\\\ y=8t, \\\\ z=2t\\end{aligned}$ \nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198228 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5524aeab-cc64-5da8-bea3-8cd5dd86ebcb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198228 #edb/ref 1074 "Substituting the expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ from the parametric equation of the line into the equation of the ellipsoid, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{24}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{24}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{6} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2} & =24 \\\\ (4t)^{2}+(8t)^{2}+4(2t)^{2} & =24 \\\\ 16{t}^{2}+64{t}^{2}+16{t}^{2} & =24 \\\\ 96{t}^{2} & =24 \\\\ {t}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solution $t = \\pm \\dfrac{1}{2}.$ \n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=-\\dfrac 1 2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=4(-\\frac{1}{2})=-2 \\\\ y=8(-\\frac{1}{2})=-4 \\\\ z=2(-\\frac{1}{2})=-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $\\left(-2,-4,-1\\right).$\n\n- For $t=\\dfrac 1 2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=4(\\frac{1}{2})=2 \\\\ y=8(\\frac{1}{2})=4 \\\\ z=2(\\frac{1}{2})=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $\\left(2,4,1\\right).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(-2,-4,-1)$ and $(2,4,1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198229 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5618" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198229 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the projection of the intersection between the ellipsoid $\\dfrac{(x+1)^2}{16}+\\dfrac{y^2}{4}+\\dfrac{z^2}{16}=1$ and the plane $x-z=3$ onto the $yz$-plane." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198229 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b1f59935-cd61-5c59-aa8d-cf7ba7f151bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198229 #edb/ref 1074 "Since we want to find the projection onto the $yz$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $x.$ First, we solve for $x$ in the equation of the plane, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-z=3\\,⟹\\,x=z+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $x$ into the equation of the ellipsoid, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{((z+3)+1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(z+4)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{z}^{2}+8z+16}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{2{z}^{2}+8z+16}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}+4z+8}{8} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by completing the square for the variable $z,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}+4z+8}{8} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{({z}^{2}+4z+4)+4}{8} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(z+2)^{2}+4}{8} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(z+2)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{1}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(z+2)^{2}}{8} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{(z+2)^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the projection of the intersection is the ellipse $\\dfrac{y^2}{2}+\\dfrac{(z+2)^2}{4} = 1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198349 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050148 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198349 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186198993 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198349 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186198998 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198349 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186338854 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198349 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186339020 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198349 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403426 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198349 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403440 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198349 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Intersection of a Surface and a Line Given in Parametric Form" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198349 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186198228 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198349 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "a426dc8c-2be0-5e83-93b6-54a6345